    93	gate PASSED under 2.3.5 (2026-08-28), making 2.3.5 the pinned authority.
    94	Every campaign-run manifest records `env_versions()` (incl. BLAS vendor and
    95	thread env vars) at runtime.
    96	
    97	## D1 — ZTF white dwarfs (anchor, done)
    98	
    99	The published 2026-08-01 bundle: 19-star truth roster + 928-star catalog.
   100	No re-run; campaign metrics re-read the published per-star JSONs.
   101	
   102	## D3 — ZTF × Kepler delta Scuti (real ZTF light curves, external labels)
   103	
   104	- Labels: Murphy+2019 (VizieR J/MNRAS/485/2380/table1, 14,330 Kepler A/F
   105	  stars; `dSct` flag 0/1/2 — ships its own labeled negative class).
   106	- Amplitude axis: Mo+2026 (J/A+A/710/A245): table2 = 259,883 extracted
   107	  frequencies (SNR>8) for 1,838 delta Scutis → per-star dominant amplitude
   108	  (ppt × 1.0857 → mmag); table1 = confirmed super-Nyquist modes → the
   109	  sub-hour stratum (any confirmed SNF ⇒ real mode above Kepler LC Nyquist
   110	  283.2 µHz ⇒ P < 59 min). This replaces the originally scouted Bowman+2016
   111	  join: Bowman's VizieR table carries no amplitudes; Mo+2026 supersedes it
   112	  (and is itself the published Murphy×Bowman merge, 1,838 stars).
   113	- Roster (`build_d3_roster.py`, rebuilt 2026-08-28 post-G1): gmag ≥ 13.2
   114	  (Murphy/KIC g magnitude — the named saturation proxy), ALL 610 dSct=1
   115	  survivors + ALL 76 dSct=2 (own class, excluded from headline numbers) +
   116	  2,314 dSct=0 negatives as a frozen-seed (20260828) simple random sample
   117	  (inclusion probability exactly 2314/7292, weight exactly 7292/2314;
   118	  sampling_weight column carried into every weighted estimate) = 3,000.
   119	  Before any campaign L-S run, the realized crossmatch mapping and an
   120	  ambiguity-adjudication file are committed (crossmatch frozen as DATA,
   121	  not just procedure). Amplitude coverage of positives:
   122	  456/610 with dominant amplitude; 48 > 10 mmag; 254 in 1–10; 154 < 1;
   123	  290 sub-hour; median 1.77 mmag. The 1–10 mmag log ladder and the
   124	  sub-threshold majority make the completeness turn-on curve the headline
   125	  D3 deliverable, not a defect (pre-registered: risk 2).
   126	- Acquisition: frozen `fetch_catalog_lightcurves.py --roster roster_d3.csv`
   127	  verbatim (10″ cone, 1.25 s cadence, resumable); frozen QC chain via
   128	  `build_panels_generic.py` (nearest-cluster crossmatch, catflags/chi cuts,
   129	  ≥20 exp/band, BJD_TDB at Palomar — all frozen functions).
   130	- Prespecified subsets: crowding (sep < 1.0″, ≤3 objects in cone),
   131	  near-saturation (g ≤ 14.0 flagged; g > 14.0 safe subset).
   132	- Caveat on record: dSct=0 means "not a delta Scuti", not "constant" — the
   133	  D3 negative-class result is a TRIGGER RATE (never called FPR); triggered
   134	  negatives get adjudicated in W4 (plausible real variable vs unexplained).
   135	
   136	## D2 — TESS-truth transplant (DAV signals in real ZTF windows)
   137	
   138	- Truth: Romero+2022 (MNRAS 511, 1574; arXiv:2201.04158; 74 new DAVs,
   139	  TESS Cy1–3) + Romero+2025 (ApJ 984, 112; arXiv:2407.07260; 32 new DAVs,
   140	  Cy4–5). Published per-mode tables: period [s] + amplitude [ppt] + per-star
   141	  FAP(1/1000) limit + 20-s-cadence flags. 2025 revisions apply: NOV
   142	  retractions (TIC 261400271, 804835539, 317620456) and updated mode lists
   143	  for re-observed 2022 objects — latest published solution wins.
   144	- Truth model, not interpolation (`d2_truth_model.py`): for 120-s sampling,
   145	  DAV P < 240 s is super-Nyquist (Nyquist period 240 s) and the boxcar
   146	  integration response has its first null at P = 120 s — two distinct
   147	  boundaries, both making interpolated TESS photometry undefined in the DAV
   148	  range; the mode table is evaluated analytically at the template's real
   149	  `bjd_tdb`. Chain: ppt → mag (×1.0857e-3) → de-dilution OFF by default
   150	  (SPOC PDCSAP is crowding-corrected; ON = prespecified variant) →
   151	  de-integrate the TESS boxcar (signed sinc; REJECT modes with
   152	  |sinc| < 0.3, i.e. P < ~160 s at 120-s cadence, P < ~27 s at 20-s);
   153	  cadence precedence is algorithmic: cadence_s = 20 iff the star's chosen
   154	  published solution includes any "f" (20-s) sector, else 120 →
   155	  bandpass ladder A_g/A_TESS ∈ {1.4, 1.7, 2.1} × A_r/A_g ∈
   156	  {0.70, 0.80, 0.90}; the blackbody T-derivative at 11,500 K gives
   157	  (1.43, 0.80) ≈ the low rung; the ADOPTED nominal (1.7, 0.80) is the grid
   158	  midpoint covering atmosphere-model/limb-darkening uncertainty (the ladder
   159	  is non-optional — zr carries most published confirmations) →
   160	  re-integrate the ZTF 30-s boxcar analytically → compose with per-mode
   161	  independent phases (PCG64(TIC), one draw per mode) shared across bands
   162	  and all variants, and a shared t_ref, so the frozen two-band rule keeps
   163	  its meaning.
   164	- Windows: templates from ALL 928 stars of the published catalog (G1 fix —
   165	  the earlier 510-not-detected pool conditioned on the pipeline's own
   166	  outcome), matched by median zg mag (|Δg| ≤ 0.25, widened when thin;
   167	  flagged), K=3 per target at 10/50/90th percentile of exposures-per-night
   168	  (75% of zg nights are single-exposure; per-night median subtraction
   169	  annihilates 53% of zg data — pre-registered, stratified: risk 3).
   170	  Template matching is fully algorithmic (zero analyst discretion): pool
   171	  filter |median_zg − target_G| ≤ 0.25, widened to 0.5 if fewer than 3
   172	  candidates, else the 9 nearest in magnitude; candidates sorted by
   173	  (median exposures-per-night, source_id); picks at indices
   174	  round(q·(n−1)) for q ∈ {0.10, 0.50, 0.90}; match label recorded.
   175	  D2 primary detection is post-injection rule firing (detection-only);
   176	  strict frequency matching is the separate frequency-recovery estimand;
   177	  native variability in the pool is contextualized by PAIRED UNINJECTED
   178	  CONTROLS (95-prefix; stable ids indexed over the sorted 928 pool): one
   179	  control shard per unique arm-B template window. W2 stretch: fetch real
   180	  ZTF light curves at the 103 Romero positions; usable self-windows form a
   181	  SEPARATE DIAGNOSTIC arm — they do not replace or enter the nominal K=3
   182	  aggregate.
   183	- Arms: B primary (signal + real ZTF mags, real magerr), A diagnostic
   184	  (synthetic Gaussian floor). Gaussian-null false-alarm rate
   185	  (`FPR_Gaussian`): 1,000 arm-A zero-amplitude simulations scheduled over
   186	  the 928-window frame by deterministic cycling (serial i → sorted-pool
   187	  window i mod 928, noise seed = serial); windows repeat, seeds do not.
   188	  Verification arm: ~20 SPOC light curves prewhitened to confirm published
   189	  solutions; everything else needs metadata only.
   190	- Run matrix (22 workers ≈ 84 runs/h). Core scheduled total ≤ 2,957 ≈
   191	  1.5 d: arm B nominal (1.7/0.80) 103×3 = 309; arm A nominal 309; Gaussian
   192	  nulls 1,000; paired controls ≤ 309 (unique arm-B windows); ladder
   193	  sensitivity MEDIAN-WINDOW-CONDITIONED: 8 non-nominal (R_g, R_rg) points
   194	  × 103 × 1 = 824; phase-draw sensitivity 2 × 103 = 206 (median window,
   195	  arm B nominal). Stretch additions listed separately: amplitude-
   196	  stationarity axis (scale × {0.7, 1.3}, median window, arm B nominal,
   197	  +206 — DAV amplitudes are nonstationary between the TESS and ZTF
   198	  epochs); Romero self-window diagnostic (count set by crossmatch yield);
   199	  de-dilution variant only for the SPOC verification-arm stars (CROWDSAP
   200	  comes with the ~20 downloads). Every sensitivity contrast uses the
   201	  common-subset rule (METRICS_SPEC).
   202	- Truth-model corrections found at implementation (2026-08-28): |sinc| ≥ 0.3
   203	  rejection corresponds to P < ~160 s at 120-s cadence (the earlier "197 s"
   204	  was the |sinc| = 0.5 point); D2 min published period is 115.9 s and 49/103
   205	  stars carry 20-s solutions, so few modes are affected. Phases are
   206	  unpublished: drawn once per star from PCG64(seed=TIC), shared across bands
   207	  and ladder variants. Blackbody derivative at 11,500 K gives (1.43, 0.80) —
   208	  the ladder's low rung; upper rungs cover atmosphere-model/limb-darkening
   209	  uncertainty.
   210	
   211	## Metrics — see METRICS_SPEC.md (frozen before any campaign L-S run)
   212	
   213	## Execution topology
   214	
   215	- Mac: rosters, fetches, shard building, metrics, figures, git (authoritative).
   216	- Laptop `jacks-7i-5090` (22 workers): replay gate + D3 run. Desktop
   217	  (needs wake; offline 64 d): D2 + D3 overflow; if unreachable, D2 runs on
   218	  the laptop after D3 (+1 day; slip rule below).
   219	- Windows job launches escape the sshd job object via WMI
   220	  `Win32_Process.Create` (Start-Process children die with the ssh session —
   221	  found the hard way on the first replay launch).
   222	- Wall model (anchor 928 ≈ 11 h at 22 workers; cost scales with baseline):
   223	  D3@3,000 ≈ 1.2–1.9 d; D2 core ≈ 1.5 d; hard stop via 150-star pilot.
   224	  Disk binds, not time: `workers = min(22, floor(free_GB × 0.5 / 0.47))`,
   225	  scratch on local NVMe/RAM disk, never a synced folder.
   226	- Results bundles: `generalization/results/<date>_<dataset>/` mirroring the
   227	  existing convention (README, DATA_PROVENANCE, SHA256SUMS, acceptance.json).
   228	
   229	## Review gates (sol@xhigh + ChatGPT Pro standing directive)
   230	
   231	| Gate | When | Reviewer | Scope |
   232	|---|---|---|---|
   233	| G1 | DONE 2026-08-28 | sol ×3 | 47 findings; dispositions in reviews/G1/RESPONSE.md; design fixes applied same day |
   234	| G2 | end W1 | sol ×5 | this file + METRICS_SPEC.md; frozen only after unanimous/addressed |
   235	| G3 | W2 pre-batch | Pro (inline code) | d2_truth_model + build_d2_shards: sinc algebra, bandpass, phase coherence, schema |
   236	| G4 | W3 mid-run | sol ×2 | pilot metrics sanity, run anomalies |
   237	| G5 | W4 | Pro + fresh-context verifier | results audit; every headline number re-derived from JSONs/CSVs |
   238	| G6 | Sep 26–29 | sol ×3 + ars-abstract | final abstract |
   239	
   240	## Timeline
   241	
   242	- W1 (Aug 28–Sep 3): tag+branch ✓, replay gate PASS 25/25 ✓ (full-928
   243	  baseline running), panel golden gate PASS both machines ✓, env pinning ✓,
   244	  frozen_api+tests ✓, D3 roster ✓, D3 IRSA fetch (overnight, running),
   245	  D2 sources downloaded ✓, PLAN+SPEC (this commit), G1, G2, D2 roster parser.
   246	- W2 (Sep 4–10): build_panels_generic on D3 → census; d2_truth_model + tests
   247	  + G3; build_d2_shards; verify_cli_identity; 150-star pilot; wake desktop.
   248	- W3 (Sep 11–17): D3 full run (laptop) ∥ D2 (desktop); metrics+plots against
   249	  pilot output; G4.
   250	- W4 (Sep 18–25): metrics, ladders, figures, bundles, acceptance; G5;
   251	  cross-dataset synthesis table.
   252	- Sep 26–30: abstract + G6; submit.
   253	- Slip rule (revised at G1 — the old "D2 alone flips the condition" claim is
   254	  untenable since D2 is not an externally labeled sample): D3 is the dataset
   255	  that satisfies the external-label condition; if only ONE new dataset can
   256	  land by Sep 25 it must be D3, with D2 stated as in progress. If only D2
   257	  lands, the abstract is scoped to injection-recovery + D1 and makes no
   258	  external-validation claim.
   259	
   260	## Top risks
   261	
   262	1. Env fails replay → pin/iterate until byte-identical; blocks all work.
   263	2. D3 completeness ≈ 0 below the a95 floor → stratification IS the
   264	   deliverable (turn-on curve).
   265	3. D2 high-pass ≈ 0 from the single-exposure-night penalty → pre-registered
   266	   expected headline, stratified to be explanatory.
   267	4. A_r/A_g lever → mandatory ladder; nominal estimate + prespecified
   268	   finite-grid sensitivity range (never called a band/CI).
   269	5. D3 negatives not constants → negative-class trigger rate with W4
   270	   adjudication (never called FPR).
   271	6. Desktop unreachable → D2 on laptop after D3 (+1 day).
   272	7. Romero mode tables are LaTeX prose with typos (comma decimals, stray
   273	   units) → parser with hard row-count and range asserts; G3 reviews the
   274	   parsed output against the PDFs.
   275	
   276	## Mandatory citations
   277	
   278	Sokolovsky+2017 (variability-index benchmark; data not public — comparison
